# Base mainnet RPC. Get a free key first -- the public endpoint
# (https://mainnet.base.org) works for a one-off read, but starts throttling
# the moment an agent polls in a loop, and a throttled RPC mid-fill looks
# exactly like a bug in your code. Alchemy (alchemy.com -> create app -> Base
# Mainnet) or Infura (infura.io -> create key -> Base) both have a free tier
# that's more than enough for a hackathon.
THETANUTS_RPC_URL=https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_KEY

# Micro-trade wallet only -- a FRESH, DISPOSABLE wallet, never one holding
# anything you'd miss. `npm i -g @thetanuts-finance/cli` then
# `thetanuts wallet create` generates one with locked-down file permissions.
# Fund it with 1-3 USDC and a few cents of ETH for gas, nothing more.
# Named THETANUTS_PRIVATE_KEY (not a generic PRIVATE_KEY) to match the SDK's
# and CLI's own convention. Never commit this -- check `git log -p` on this
# file before you submit, same as the official checklist says.
THETANUTS_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# Must match gate-chain/server.py's bind address/port.
GATE_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# Port the execution/ HTTP API (src/api/server.ts) listens on -- this is
# what the frontend calls (GET /orders, GET /market-data, POST /propose,
# POST /execute). Distinct from the gate chain's own port above.
API_PORT=8790

# Hard ceiling enforced client-side in executeMicroTrade.ts, independent of
# the gate chain's own MAX_NOTIONAL_USD_PER_TRADE -- belt and suspenders
# before anything reaches a signer. "1-3 USDC covers you" per the workshop
# deck; a 1 USDC fill scores identically to a 100 USDC one, so there's no
# reason to raise this for the demo.
MAX_NOTIONAL_USD_HARD_CAP=3

# Required for POST /converse (src/copilot.ts) -- the natural-language layer
# in front of the gate chain. Any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions
# endpoint works. This LLM never approves a trade -- see copilot.ts's header
# comment.
#
# Two independent provider slots, not one shared model: PARSE_LLM_* drives
# parseIntent, which runs on every message including every round of a
# multi-turn clarification exchange -- keep this one fast. EXPLAIN_LLM_*
# drives explainDecision, which runs once after the gate chain has already
# decided -- the frontend renders the PASS/FAIL result before this call's
# prose even arrives, so a slower/cheaper model costs little felt latency
# here. Each EXPLAIN_LLM_* falls back to its PARSE_LLM_* counterpart if
# unset, so a single-provider setup only needs the PARSE_LLM_* three below.
PARSE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
PARSE_LLM_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY
PARSE_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# Optional: point explanations at a different (e.g. larger/cheaper/shared-
# capacity) provider, such as Featherless AI (https://api.featherless.ai/v1).
# EXPLAIN_LLM_DISABLE_THINKING=true only for hybrid-reasoning models (e.g.
# Qwen3) that emit a <think>...</think> block by default -- harmless no-op
# otherwise.
# EXPLAIN_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.featherless.ai/v1
# EXPLAIN_LLM_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY
# EXPLAIN_LLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
# EXPLAIN_LLM_DISABLE_THINKING=true
